                <pb facs="0129" n="41" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg41"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.5151/122: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Morgan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-21T17:00:00-05:00">February 21, 1933—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>37. The Department approves the procedure proposed in the first two sentences of
                    the last paragraph of your No. 4028, February 2, 1933, regarding exchange
                    restrictions and hopes you will take early opportunity to discuss this matter
                    with Brazilian authorities. It does not, however, believe that the proposal in
                    the second numbered paragraph of the memorandum mentioned in the last sentence
                    of your despatch would be advantageous to the interests of this country, all
                    things being considered.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
